※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4630 LANG_HANDED_OUT_IN_AFTER_CALL

※ `EXPR in NAME` says an expression takes its room from an arena that already exists; a call that
※ hands out an arena of its own makes it, and a definition receives it.

fn named(n: u64) → str in pool:
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    "a" ⧺ "b" in pool

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let k: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(k)
    let s: str = named(1u64) in k
    if s = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
